  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ef4120e8d7cc4784ba80e7aeb2d6d58d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Bragi_Ending_Death
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Repeatable: 0
  Lines:
  - Text: Oftentimes, stories have no audience. That is what I devoted my life to;
      telling those stories. Our most beautiful lie was to be one of those stories.
      Born of poison and blood, the Child of Lies faced challenges three and even
      struck down the storyteller, who broke his oath to try to stop the subject
      of his story.
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: "Ah, the beauty of it all. I weep at the thought of what might come next.
      I reckon\u2026 the little Lie enters the cave where the Father of Lies is trapped,
      and in the presence of his saviour, the chains break. Loki falls to the ground,
      and Sigyn is there to catch him. She weeps as he weeps, and the Lie falls to
      their knees as they are overwhelmed by the sight."
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: Thank you, newborn child, for saving us.
    Speaker: 7
  - Text: '*Unintelligible*'
    Speaker: 6
  - Text: "Father, mother\u2026 I am back."
    Speaker: 0
  - Text: I wonder, would Sigyn and Loki open their arms to let this child into their
      family, or would they scorn them and consider them a facsimile of the children
      Loki truly lost.
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: Oh, child, I am sorry for having forced this trial upon you. We love you
      so for the freedom you have brought us.
    Speaker: 7
  - Text: "Yes, I do not believe Sigyn could ever reject a child in front of her,
      she is too loving for that. Loki might be broken by the torture, but he would
      recover and speak in due time, I\u2019m sure."
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: "You\u2026 you are not my Fenrir or my Hel. I see\u2026 you\u2026 child
      of mine\u2026"
    Speaker: 6
  - Text: "Yes, I believe that is how this story goes on. Ah, if only I had not been
      killed. I would have loved to see Ragnar\xF6k too, for the story that ends
      the world must be the most beautiful one."
    Speaker: 2
  - Text: "Little Lie, when you see Ragnar\xF6k happen because of your own actions,
      will you record the tale in my honour? Will you tell the world that you set
      its demise into action, or will you fight to defy the undefiable destiny? The
      stage is set and we\u2019re entering our third act, it would seem"
    Speaker: 2
